0000              1   ; ISR_example_DE10Lite.asm:
0000              2   ; a) Increments/decrements a BCD variable every half second using
0000              3   ;    an ISR for timer 2.  Uses SW0 to decide.  Also 'blinks' LEDR0 every
0000              4   ;    half second.
0000              5   ; b) Generates a 2kHz square wave at pin P1.5 using an ISR for timer 0.
0000              6   ; c) In the 'main' loop it displays the variable incremented/decremented
0000              7   ;    using the ISR for timer 2 on the LCD and the 7-segment displays.
0000              8   ;    Also resets it to zero if the KEY1 pushbutton  is pressed.
0000              9   ; d) Controls the LCD using general purpose pins P2.3, P2.5, P2.7, P3.1, P3.3, P3.5, P3.7
0000             10   ;
0000             11   ; FIXES ADDED:
0000             12   ;   1) Stack pointer moved off 0x7F -> 0x60 (0x7F causes pushes into SFR space at 0x80+)
0000             13   ;   2) Removed cpl P1.1 inside Timer2 ISR (P1.1 is LCD E pin, was being toggled every 1ms)
0000             14   ;   3) Timer2 ISR now saves/restores B, DPL, DPH too (prevents random corruption w/ math/LCD)
0000             15   ;   4) Serial: setb TI after init, and a more standard putchar (wait TI, clr TI, write SBUF)
0000             16   ;
0000             17   ; EXTRA FIXES (for your errors):
0000             18   ;   5) Renamed Wait25ms labels (W25_L1/W25_L2/W25_L3) so they don't conflict with LCD delays (L1/L2/L3).
0000             19   ;   6) Removed the illegal "mov a, a" bug that caused parse/register errors.
0000             20   ;   7) Added keypad-driven parameter UI in State 0 (edit soak/reflow temps/times).
0000             21   ;
